  <section class="section"><div class="container detail-grid"><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Our role</span><h3 style="margin-top:16px">The right specialists, coordinated around your needs.</h3><p>We help clients identify the questions to ask and connect with experienced, independent professionals.</p><a class="btn" href="/#contact">Start a conversation <span>↗</span></a></aside><div class="detail-copy"><p class="lead">Tax planning should be personal, cross-border aware and led by qualified advisers.</p><p>We can coordinate introductions to established Italian tax advisers, lawyers and wealth-planning professionals whose expertise matches your circumstances. This can be especially relevant when considering a change of tax residence, the acquisition of Italian property or the interaction between international assets and Italian rules.</p><h2>Italy’s €300,000 flat-tax regime</h2><p>Italy offers an optional lump-sum substitute tax regime for certain individuals who transfer their tax residence to Italy. For eligible individuals transferring residence from 1 January 2026, the annual substitute tax on qualifying foreign-source income is €300,000; qualifying family members may be included for an additional annual amount of €50,000 each. Different amounts may continue to apply to people who transferred residence in earlier years.</p><p>The regime is subject to eligibility requirements, including a test relating to Italian tax residence in the previous ten tax periods. It concerns qualifying foreign-source income and should not be understood as a blanket tax on all income or as an automatic benefit for every new resident. The correct treatment depends on the individual facts and current law.</p><h2>How we support the process</h2><ul><li>Help define the questions and objectives before a relocation or property commitment.</li><li>Coordinate introductions to qualified tax, legal and wealth-planning professionals.</li><li>Help align property decisions, project timing and the wider relocation plan.</li><li>Maintain a clear distinction between project coordination and regulated professional advice.</li></ul><div class="callout"><strong>Important</strong><p style="margin:8px 0 0">Lake Como Property Advisory does not provide tax or legal opinions. Tax eligibility, structuring and filing must be assessed by a qualified professional based on the client's circumstances and the law in force.</p></div><p style="margin-top:30px"><a class="text-link" href="/journal/italy-flat-tax-300000-euro/">Read our introduction to the €300,000 flat tax <span>↗</span></a></p></div></div></section>
